// La Grass-Hopper (Ch1, MAP_BOIS_ETHER_GYM): Loic's gym inside the giant hollow tree.
// contenu-jeu/chapitres/01-bois-ether.md §4: the inside of the trunk turned into decompression
// airlocks (spore grates, a shower, round hatches) and a tinkerer's workshop (workbenches, vices,
// flower pots plugged into power strips, hanging tools), up to a greenhouse under a small glass
// dome ("a dome in the Dome") where potted plants feed a big central pipe.
// The primary (Building) has no floor metatile, so this spec has no ground: textures are opaque,
// and the objects' art is composited after prep over the texture it stands on (`sol`, `sol_serre`,
// the wall `mur`, the glass wall `verriere`), so that no cell keeps a transparent pixel.
// The airlock doors are two cells (top, bottom), closed and open variants (ch01_gym.rs).
// `mur` comes before `bois`: a 1x1 stamp of metatile 513 would equal the extract's
// Route104_Prototype layout (studio map hygiene).
(
    name: "SilBoisEtherGym",
    primary: "Building",
    ground: None,
    style: "Minimalist 16-bit sprite in the Pokemon Ruby/Emerald indoor style (Game Boy Advance), seen from the top-down three-quarter view of Pokemon games. Simple, iconic, low detail: big flat colour areas, 2-3 shades per material, a 1-pixel dark outline, no texture noise, no gradients, no tiny decorations, no anti-aliasing.",
    features: [
        (
            name: "sol",
            cells: ["."],
            key: Some("none"),
            prompt: Some("Indoor floor texture seen from above, only 16x16 pixels, chunky details: smooth light honey-coloured wood, the flat cut surface of a tree with two faint darker growth-ring arcs. It must tile seamlessly in every direction."),
        ),
        (
            name: "mur",
            cells: ["#", "#"],
            key: Some("none"),
            prompt: Some("An indoor wall segment seen from the front, one tile wide and two tiles tall: the inside of a hollow tree trunk, vertical brown bark planks, a horizontal copper pipe with a bolt running across the upper half from the left edge to the right edge, a darker brown skirting band at the bottom. It must tile seamlessly from left to right."),
        ),
        (
            name: "bois",
            cells: ["#"],
